# Premium feature copy sync

When Premium capabilities change (add/remove/rename a feature, change free vs paid limits, or change what full plan / «Оплатить только нужные функции» unlocks), update **all** user-facing copy in the same change.

## Single source of truth

| What | Where |
|------|--------|
| Feature ids (order) | `FEATURE_IDS` / `purchasable_feature_ids()` in [`premium.py`](premium.py) |
| Short name (buttons, lists, full-plan bullets) | `premium_feat_<id>` in `locales/ru.json` + `locales/en.json` |
| Longer explanation (à la carte pick screen) | `premium_feat_<id>_desc` (same locales) |
| Full-plan screen assembly | `premium_benefits_text()` + `premium_title` (`{benefits}`) in [`premium_handlers.py`](premium_handlers.py) |
| Streamer channel line (not in FEATURE_IDS) | `premium_channel_benefit` |

Do **not** hardcode a parallel feature list inside `premium_title` or README that can drift from `premium_feat_*`.

## Checklist

1. **Code** — `FEATURE_IDS` / gates / `feature_label_key` mapping updated.
2. **Locales** — for each id: `premium_feat_<id>` + `premium_feat_<id>_desc` in **ru and en**. Remove obsolete keys.
3. **Screens** — full Premium (`premium_benefits_text`) and «Оплатить только нужные функции» (`_premium_feat_pick_text`) both resolve names via `feature_label_key` / `feature_desc_key`.
4. **README** — if the product surface table mentions Premium capabilities, update [`README.md`](README.md) + [`README.en.md`](README.en.md) ([`readme.mdc`](readme.mdc)).
5. **self_check** — extend assertions that every purchasable id has label+desc and appears in `premium_benefits_text` (see `checks_handlers.py`).

## Skip

Internal refactors with no user-visible Premium wording change.
